     [38;5;246mNew src/tracking.js with trackEvent(name, payload); writes to console today, swappable for a real backend later [39m
     [38;5;246mwithout touching call sites.[39m
  [38;5;246m2.[39m Just console.log the userId
     [38;5;246mNo new structure. Include userId in the existing log line. Useful for dev visibility only; nothing is durable.[39m
  [38;5;246m3.[39m POST to a real endpoint
     [38;5;246mSend login events to an analytics/backend URL. Answers "who logged in" for real; needs an endpoint, failure [39m
